As for copyrights, you need to look at A) the licensing agreement of
*all* of your sounds (read carefully), since you're ripping them from
others, and B) pay special attention to those that you took lock,
stock, and barrel.  The Zelda secret door thing, for example would
definitely not be fair use; you're using the whole clip.

Making your own sfx isn't that hard, and can actually be kind of fun.
Look around your house.  Crinkling up paper rapidly and continuously
can sound like a fire, for example.  You may find that you can get a
lot stranger sounds out of your throat than you knew possible, even
before effects - after special effects, you're left with some really
interesting stuff.  :)



